<title>USA: U.S. Q2 non-farm productivity rev to up 0.5 pct.</title>
<headline>U.S. Q2 non-farm productivity rev to up 0.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Labor Dept revised estimates of Q2 1996 U.S. productivity/costs, seasonally adjusted annual percent changes from prior quarters, on chain weights basis:</p>
<p>    -	     - Productivity -	  - - -Output- - -</p>
<p>    -	     Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1	  Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1</p>
<p> NonFarm	   0.5  -0.1   1.8	   4.9   4.2   2.7</p>
<p> Manufacturing   2.2   1.5   5.6	   6.4   5.5   2.4</p>
<p> Durable Goods   3.9   3.1   7.8	  10.9  10.0   5.5</p>
<p> NonDurables     0.5  -0.1   2.9	   0.9   0.1  -1.5</p>
<p> Total Business  1.1   0.5   2.0	   5.2   4.4   3.0</p>
<p>P-Preliminary. R-Revised.</p>
<p>    -	     - - -Hours- - -	Hourly Compensation</p>
<p>    -	     Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1	  Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1</p>
<p> NonFarm	   4.4   4.3   1.0	   3.7   3.7   3.3</p>
<p> Manufacturing   4.1   3.9  -3.0	   5.8   5.8   0.4</p>
<p> Durable Goods   6.8   6.6  -2.1	   6.8   6.8  -2.2</p>
<p> NonDurables     0.4   0.2  -4.3	   3.9   3.8   4.6</p>
<p> Total Business  4.0   3.9   1.0	   4.0   4.1   3.0</p>
<p>P-Preliminary. R-Revised.  </p>
<p>    -	 Real Hourly Compensation    Unit Labor Costs</p>
<p>    -	     Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1	  Q2-R  Q2-P    Q1</p>
<p> NonFarm	  -0.1  -0.1  UNCH	   3.2   3.8   1.5</p>
<p> Manufacturing   1.9   1.9  -2.8	   3.6   4.2  -4.9</p>
<p> Durable Goods   2.8   2.8  -5.3	   2.8   3.5  -9.3</p>
<p> NonDurables    UNCH  UNCH   1.3	   3.4   3.9   1.6</p>
<p> Total Business  0.2   0.2  -0.2	   2.9   3.6   1.0</p>
<p>P-Preliminary. R-Revised.</p>
<p>Wall Street economists had forecast second quarter non-farm productivity to be revised to up 0.4 percent.</p>
<p>Compared to the second quarter of 1995, non-farm productivity rose 0.8 percent in the second quarter, output rose 3.2 percent, hours increased 2.4 percent, hourly compensation grew 3.8 percent, real compensation increased 0.9 percent and unit labor costs rose 2.9 percent, the department said.</p>
